    "justification": "The lemma supplies a branch-valid and center-coherent score on PT-only and SC-only local sequences, so the attainment target never invokes an intersection-only object off the intersection.",
    "gap": "SunXieZhang2025 gives separate branch scores, but does not construct a fixed-rank continuation from their common intersection score into both local charts.",
    "consumer": "The chart extension is the score target needed for one branch-robust interval under local switching in the Alaska and sugary-drink-tax panels.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix a branch \\(b\\) and a nearby \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_b\\).  By the tangent normal form,\n\\[\n \\mathcal I_b(P)=\\sum_xg_{b,x}(P)+\\operatorname{span}\\{R_{b,x}(P):x\\in\\mathcal X\\}.\n \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe coefficients \\(a_x^U(P_0)\\) and \\(d_x^U(P_0)\\) in Definition \\(\\mathrm{def{:}local\\text{-}score\\text{-}extension}\\) are fixed finite vectors.  Substitution in (1) proves \\(\\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P;b,P_0)\\in\\mathcal I_b(P)\\).  At \\(P=P_0\\), the two formulas are the two equal representations selected by \\(\\mathrm{QP}_x\\); the union theorem therefore gives\n\\[\n \\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P_0;\\mathrm{PT},P_0)\n =\\phi_U(P_0)\n =\\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P_0;\\mathrm{SC},P_0).\n \\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nIt remains to prove the rate rather than assert continuity.  The QMD condition and its bounded score norm imply\n\\[\n \\left\\|\\sqrt{dP_{n,O}/dP_{0,O}}-1\\right\\|_{L^2(P_{0,O})}=O(n^{-1/2}).\n \\tag{3}\n\\]\nFor a cell indicator times \\(Y_t^k\\), \\(k=0,1,2\\), Cauchy--Schwarz applied to the factorization of the difference of the two densities gives\n\\[\n |E_{P_{n,O}}f-E_{P_{0,O}}f|\n \\le\n \\left\\|\\sqrt{dP_{n,O}/dP_{0,O}}-1\\right\\|_2\n \\left\\{E_{P_{n,O}}[f^2]+E_{P_{0,O}}[f^2]\n +2(E_{P_{n,O}}[f^2]E_{P_{0,O}}[f^2])^{1/2}\\right\\}^{1/2}.\n \\tag{4}\n\\]\nThe fourth-moment envelope makes the second factor bounded, and cell mass and overlap permit division by all relevant cell probabilities.  Hence every cell probability, conditional mean, and conditional second moment entering \\(g_{b,x}\\), \\(R_{b,x}\\), and \\(\\Omega_x\\) differs from its value at \\(P_0\\) by \\(O(n^{-1/2})\\).\n\nThe inverse \\((B'B)^{-1}\\) is locally Lipschitz because its least eigenvalue is at least \\(\\kappa_0\\).  Likewise, after retaining the fixed independent coordinates, inversion on the nonzero Gram eigenspace is locally Lipschitz because \\(\\lambda_{\\min}^+(\\Omega_x)\\ge\\kappa_0\\) and rank is constant.  The finite-cell influence formulas are affine in the observed residuals with coefficients that are smooth functions of the moments just listed.  Equations (3)--(4) and the second-moment bound therefore imply, for either chart,\n\\[\n \\|\\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P_n;b,P_0)-\n   \\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P_0;b,P_0)\\|_{L^2(P_{n,O})}\n =O(n^{-1/2}).\n \\tag{5}\n\\]\nWhen both labels are admissible, subtract (5) for the two branches and use the common center equality (2).  The triangle inequality yields\n\\[\n \\|\\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P_n;\\mathrm{PT},P_0)-\n   \\phi_U^{\\mathrm{loc}}(P_n;\\mathrm{SC},P_0)\\|_{L^2(P_{n,O})}\n =O(n^{-1/2}),\n\\]\nas required.  All constants may depend on the fixed sequence's QMD score bound; the lemma does not claim a supremum over sequences.",
